The task is to implement a Verilog module `TopModule` that monitors a 32-bit input `in`. For each bit, if it changes from 1 in one clock cycle to 0 in the next, the corresponding bit in the output `out` should be set to 1 and remain 1 until a synchronous `reset` (active high) is applied.

The implementation uses a register `in_prev` to store the value of `in` from the previous clock cycle. On each positive edge of the clock, it checks if a bit was 1 in `in_prev` and is now 0 in `in` (i.e., `in_prev & ~in`). If this condition is met, the corresponding bit in `out` is updated using an OR operation (`out | (in_prev & ~in)`), ensuring that once a bit is set to 1, it stays 1. The `reset` signal is handled synchronously.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input reset,
    input [31:0] in,
    output reg [31:0] out
);

    reg [31:0] in_prev;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset) begin
            out <= 32'b0;
            in_prev <= in;
        end else begin
            in_prev <= in;
            out <= out | (in_prev & ~in);
        end
    end

endmodule
```
